  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The radius of the largest sphere which fits properly at the centre of the edge of a body centred cubic unit cell is :\r\n\r\n(Edge length is represented by 'a')",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rAKx6",
      "text": "0.027 a",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9mpLN",
      "text": "0.047 a",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2yRHy",
      "text": "$0.134 \\mathrm{a}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5VxbZ",
      "text": "0.067 a",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For bcc\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{a}}{4}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\text { Empty space at edge }=a-2 R=a-\\frac{\\sqrt{3} a}{2}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n$=$ diameter of sphere.\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{r}_{\\text {sphere }}=\\frac{a-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\mathrm{a}}{2}=\\left(\\frac{2-\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right) \\mathrm{a}=0.067 \\mathrm{a}\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
